  "chapters": [
    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "PHM",
      "chapter": 1,
      "chapter_usfm": "PHM.1",
      "version_id": 68,
      "version_abbr": "GNT",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "From Paul, a prisoner for the sake of Christ Jesus, and from our brother Timothy—To our friend and fellow worker Philemon,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and the church that meets in your house, and our sister Apphia, and our fellow soldier Archippus:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "May God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ give you grace and peace."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Brother Philemon, every time I pray, I mention you and give thanks to my God."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For I hear of your love for all of God's people and the faith you have in the Lord Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "My prayer is that our fellowship with you as believers will bring about a deeper understanding of every blessing which we have in our life in union with Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Your love, dear brother, has brought me great joy and much encouragement! You have cheered the hearts of all of God's people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this reason I could be bold enough, as your brother in Christ, to order you to do what should be done."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But because I love you, I make a request instead. I do this even though I am Paul, the ambassador of Christ Jesus, and at present also a prisoner for his sake."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So I make a request to you on behalf of Onesimus, who is my own son in Christ; for while in prison I have become his spiritual father."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "At one time he was of no use to you, but now he is useful both to you and to me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I am sending him back to you now, and with him goes my heart."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I would like to keep him here with me, while I am in prison for the gospel's sake, so that he could help me in your place."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "However, I do not want to force you to help me; rather, I would like for you to do it of your own free will. So I will not do anything unless you agree."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "It may be that Onesimus was away from you for a short time so that you might have him back for all time."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And now he is not just a slave, but much more than a slave: he is a dear brother in Christ. How much he means to me! And how much more he will mean to you, both as a slave and as a brother in the Lord!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So, if you think of me as your partner, welcome him back just as you would welcome me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "If he has done you any wrong or owes you anything, charge it to my account."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Here, I will write this with my own hand: I, Paul, will pay you back. (I should not have to remind you, of course, that you owe your very self to me.)"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So, my brother, please do me this favor for the Lord's sake; as a brother in Christ, cheer me up!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I am sure, as I write this, that you will do what I ask—in fact I know that you will do even more."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "At the same time, get a room ready for me, because I hope that God will answer the prayers of all of you and give me back to you."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Epaphras, who is in prison with me for the sake of Christ Jesus, sends you his greetings,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and so do my co-workers Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke."
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with you all."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 25,
      "headings": [
